<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Malbak yr shr pre-exceps rises, div up.</title>
<headline>Malbak yr shr pre-exceps rises, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Aug 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-exceps	 191.0	 vs 164.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 58.0	  vs 46.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   643.0	 vs 510.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1,093.0     vs 967.0</p>
<p>    Effect tax rate (pct) 28.9	  vs 28.4</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   194.0	 vs 156.0</p>
<p>    Turnover		  17,649.0    vs 15,508.0</p>
<p>Full name: Malbak Ltd (industrial holding)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     34.0 loss   vs 56.0 profit</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 9</p>
<p>on register Nov 15</p>
<p>NOTE -  Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings of between 181.3 and 184.0 cents a share, with consensus at 182.1 cents. They expected a dividend of 51.4 cents.</p>
<p>The exceptional loss rose primarily from factory closures and healthcare related losses, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
